From 4ca0e51396c24aa47891ac59f1b93bcd7c724882 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Velle Sinclair <brncomputerhelp@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 19:53:11 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 42/42] fix(shaders): a const local may take a value known only
 at run time

HLSL's const only makes a local read-only, so effects set const locals
from uniforms. GLSL 330 wants a constant expression there, and the
layer failed to compile. The ASCII-art filter (workshop 2582854209)
sizes its character grid that way, so 3593224238 showed its planet
without the filter it is built around.

The shader header now enables GL_ARB_shading_language_420pack, which
allows it. Only glslang reads the header; the driver is handed the
GLSL 330 that SPIRV-Cross writes out, so it needs nothing new.

The new tests compile both HLSL habits the corpus relies on through
the shader units: this one, and math on two vectors of different
sizes, which the glslang patch shipped alongside narrows. A shape
HLSL rejects too still fails.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
